Suppose that $x$ is an integer that satisfies the following congruences: \begin{align*}
3+x &\equiv 2^2 \pmod{3^3} \\
5+x &\equiv 3^2 \pmod{5^3} \\
7+x &\equiv 5^2 \pmod{7^3}
\end{align*}What is the remainder when $x$ is divided by $105$?

s:
A number is congruent to the sum of its digits $\pmod 9$. Thus, \begin{align*}
1+22+333&+4444+55555+666666+7777777+88888888\\ &\equiv 1+4+9+16+25+36+49+64 \\
&\equiv 1+4+0+7+7+0+4+1 \\
&= 24 \\
&\equiv \boxed{6}\pmod 9.
\end{align*}

The prime factorization of $432 = 2^4 \cdot 3^3$. It follows that the sum of the divisors is equal to $(1 + 2 + 2^2 + 2^3 + 2^4)(1 + 3 + 3^2 + 3^3)$, as each factor of $432$ is represented when the product is expanded. We have to subtract $432$ so that we only count the proper divisors, so the answer is \begin{align*}
(1 + 2 + 4 + 8 + 16)(1 + 3 + 9 + 27) - 432 &= (31)(40) - 432\\
&= 1240 - 432\\
&= \boxed{808}.\\
\end{align*}

Note that $34 \equiv -13 \pmod{47}$.  Hence, \begin{align*}
34^{-1} &\equiv (-13)^{-1} \\
&\equiv (-1)^{-1} \cdot 13^{-1} \\
&\equiv (-1) \cdot 29 \\
&\equiv \boxed{18} \pmod{47}.
\end{align*}

